WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.850
DNA is the genetic material in every
cell that is passed from generation to

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.200
generation. Each cell has a lot of DNA,
and it needs to be organized to make it

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.640
easy to inherit. But how is your DNA
organized? DNA in cells exists in

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.310
discrete units called chromosomes. Each
chromosome is made up of one very, very,

5
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:24.070
very long piece of double stranded DNA
that has thousands of genes. Your cells

6
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.420
have 46 chromosomes and they come in
pairs, 23 that you inherited from your

7
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.530
biological mother and a matching pair
of 23 chromosomes from your biological

8
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.710
father. Thus, most of your genes come
in duplicates, a copy from mom and a

9
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.820
copy from dad. If you accidentally
inherit one too little or one too many

10
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:46.130
chromosomes, consequences can be severe.
For example, Down syndrome occurs when

11
00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:50.450
you have three, instead of two, copies
of chromosome 21. One pair of

12
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.510
chromosomes is unique and is involved
in determining your sex. If you inherit

13
00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.840
an X chromosome from mom and an X from
dad, you are a double X and acquire the

14
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.310
characteristic traits of a female. If
you acquire the puny little Y

15
00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:06.790
chromosome from dad then you are an XY
and become a male. Different organisms

16
00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.640
have different numbers of chromosomes.
Some plants have hundreds of

17
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.570
chromosomes, and some ants have only
one pair. In addition to their role in

18
00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.850
heredity, chromosomes are a way of
packaging a long string of DNA in a

19
00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:25.180
small, small space. In animals, fungi,
and plants, DNA is stored in a membrane

20
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.470
structure called the nucleus. If we
blow up a nucleus 10,000 times its

21
00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:33.490
size, then it would fit half the width
of this paper. On this scale, your DNA

22
00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:37.710
in total would be 20 kilometers long,
and would have to fit into this space

23
00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.290
without getting tangled. In chromosomes,
special proteins called histones act

24
00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:46.440
like spools to wrap and help neatly
package DNA. Want to learn more about

25
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.890
how chromosomes are inherited? See our
videos on mitosis and meiosis.

